+ * the gate plainly, then plants every row of `check-favicon.plants.mjs` in memory (each must RED
+ * exactly its clause set and the check ids it names; the negative-negatives must stay GREEN), then
+ * the EDGES (every numeric bound pinned by a plant within ε each side, sought on the gate's own
+ * reading) and the CUTS (every cut inside tie() pinned by a plant at cut ± ε/2). `--sabotage-battery`
+ * switches each check off in turn, and each library clause the gate reads, and the self-test must red
+ * every time; `--threshold-battery` moves each bound and each cut by its ε both ways, and every move
+ * must red. Run: `node scripts/check-favicon.self-test.mjs [--sabotage-battery |
+ * --threshold-battery] [--root <web/frontend>]`.
